WEBVTT

00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:31.170
it's not just a thought experiment,
although it is that,

00:01:31.212 --> 00:01:32.421
but it's more.

00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:34.090
It could have tangible effects.

00:01:34.757 --> 00:01:38.344
If we're willing to inspect
what actually spikes our heart rate

00:01:38.386 --> 00:01:40.638
and pushes us to the edge of our seats,

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.932
instead of just assuming we know,

00:01:42.932 --> 00:01:47.979
we can all, collectively, make
the sports world a more equitable place.

00:01:48.646 --> 00:01:51.107
I didn't say "equal," I said "equitable."

00:01:51.107 --> 00:01:53.985
Fair, evenhanded, just.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:59.323
Often, if you ask someone
why they watch sports,

00:01:59.365 --> 00:02:02.618
they will tell you because they want
to watch the best of the best.